**Terms of Service — Alongside: Move**

**Effective date: ****[DATE — to be set on publication]****
Business: **Build New Habits (Graeme Wright, sole trader). **HMRC registration in progress.****
Contact: **hello@buildnewhabits.co.uk

Please read these Terms carefully before using Alongside: Move. By creating an account, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the app.

## **1. What Alongside Is — and Is Not**

Alongside: Move is a fitness coaching application that adapts to how you feel each day. It is designed for general fitness, health, and wellbeing purposes. It does not diagnose, treat, monitor, or prevent any medical condition, and is not intended to be regulated as a medical device. It is not a medical application and does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. If you have medical concerns, consult a doctor before starting any exercise programme.

Alongside is designed to reduce risk through condition safety filtering, but no software can guarantee safety for every individual in every circumstance. You are responsible for your own physical safety. Stop any activity that causes pain and seek medical attention if required.

## **2. Accounts and Eligibility**

To use Alongside, you must be **at least 18 years of age**. We ask for your date of birth when you create your account to confirm this. You are responsible for all activity under your account; keep your access secure and do not share it with others.

We reserve the right to suspend or terminate accounts that violate these Terms or that we believe could harm the service or other users.

## **3. Subscriptions and Payment**

### **Free tier**

Alongside is available free of charge with a permanent free tier. Safety-critical features — including burnout detection, Recovery Mode, and condition safety filtering — are never paywalled.

### **The Plan**

- Monthly: £7.99/month. **No introductory rate** — the price you see is the price you pay from the first payment onward.

- Annual: £59.99/year.

- Beta participants: a permanently locked annual rate of £44.99/year, available **during December 2026 only**. Once taken, this rate is held for as long as the subscription runs.

- Community organisation members: access via a unique code issued to partner organisations, at rates set out at the time of the partnership.

- **Your rate never rises.** If we change our prices, you keep the rate you joined at for as long as your subscription runs. Any change applies only to people joining after it.

- **[YEAR 2 PRICING — deliberately not set. To be decided in Year 2 in light of real data, and in any case subject to the rate-never-rises commitment above.]**

### **Free trial**

- **30 days free.** Card details are taken at signup and no payment is made during the trial.

- You'll be reminded before the trial ends and told exactly what you'll be charged and when.

- Cancel at any point during the trial and you will not be charged at all.

### **Auto-renewal**

Your subscription renews automatically at the end of each billing period unless you cancel first. You'll receive an email reminder 7 days before each annual renewal. Cancel any time from Settings → Subscription.

Annual subscriptions renew on the anniversary of your first payment.

### **Refund policy**

Under UK Consumer Contracts Regulations, you can cancel and receive a full refund within 14 days of the contract being concluded, unless you've actively used the subscription during that period, in which case we apply a pro-rata refund for unused days.

**[FOR SOLICITOR REVIEW — the interaction between the free trial and the statutory cooling-off period. Our understanding is that the 14-day CCR period runs from the day the contract is concluded (signup), not from the day payment is first taken — so on a trial the statutory right may already have expired at the moment of the first charge. We propose offering a voluntary 14-day full-refund right running from the FIRST PAYMENT, in addition to the statutory right, so that nobody is charged at a point where they have no way out. Please confirm this is the correct construction and that offering a more generous voluntary right does not complicate the statutory position.]**

After that, subscriptions are non-refundable, though you can cancel any time to stop future renewals. If a technical fault prevented you from using the service, contact hello@buildnewhabits.co.uk for a full refund.

## **4. Your Data**

How we handle your personal and health information is described in full in our Privacy Policy, which forms part of these Terms. By agreeing to these Terms, you confirm you've read and understood the Privacy Policy.

## **5. Intellectual Property**

All content within Alongside — including coaching scripts, the exercise library, the applied psychological frameworks, the design system, and source code — is the intellectual property of Build New Habits (Graeme Wright). **Ownership of certain visual assets, including the current product logo, is subject to a separate legal review — see the accompanying IP/trademark question sheet.** You may not reproduce, distribute, modify, or create derivative works from any part of Alongside without written permission.

## **6. Limitation of Liability**

Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, or for any other liability that cannot be excluded or limited under UK law. Subject to that, we are not liable for any physical injury resulting from exercise activities, including those recommended by the app. We are not liable for loss of data, though we take reasonable steps to protect it per our Privacy Policy. Subject to the first sentence of this section, our total liability to you for any claim under these Terms will not exceed the amount you've paid us in the 12 months before the claim.

## **7. Changes to These Terms**

We may update these Terms from time to time. For material changes, we'll notify you by email at least 14 days before they take effect.

## **8. Governing Law**

These Terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and any disputes are subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales.

